(7054858, 1072632, 115814, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by giantmike:</b></div><hr/><i> The focus feels just the slightest bit off. I want the beans/sugar to be tack sharp, but what I''m seeing is the cup handle tack sharp. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I''ve been frustrated with what seems to be an inevitable loss of sharpness when posting here. I''m using CS5 to resize my images to the max allowable 800 px with bicubic sharper option. This seems to create a better version than what I see once uploaded to DPC. Any suggestions out there?</td>', 'Originally posted by giantmike: The focus feels just the slightest bit off. I want the beans/sugar to be tack sharp, but what I''m seeing is the cup handle tack sharp.   I''ve been frustrated with what seems to be an inevitable loss of sharpness when posting here. I''m using CS5 to resize my images to the max allowable 800 px with bicubic sharper option. This seems to create a better version than what I see once uploaded to DPC. Any suggestions out there?', '2013-06-25 02:55:52.000000', NULL, 0),
